{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming 099e4c83. Re-derived on current main 7e7b8412; the request describes the world at a7a9abe7.\n\nThe defect is present and total, not partial. internal/statusview/view.go:144 normalizes with strings.Join(strings.Fields(value), \" \"). Fields splits on Unicode whitespace, and ESC (0x1b), BEL (0x07), the other C0/C1 controls, and the bidi overrides (U+202A-202E, U+2066-2069) are not whitespace. Every one of them passes through unchanged into terminal-facing output. I already have direct evidence rather than inference: the bounded-status work I merged as e9ec6070 carries a hostile-projection fixture whose strings embed ESC[2J ESC[1;1H, BEL, and a bidi override in every user-controlled field, and the golden output records those bytes surviving intact. That fixture currently documents the hole; this work closes it and the fixture becomes the regression.\n\nWhat I will do: render those characters visibly and unambiguously in human-facing text while leaving the durable bytes and the JSON meaning untouched -- the log is the record and must not be rewritten to suit a renderer. I will cover every caller of the shared normalization path rather than the one in front of me, and check for a second expression of the same rule elsewhere before calling it done. Byte and rune caps stay valid after escaping, which is the part most likely to break quietly: escaping lengthens strings, so the cap arithmetic has to be re-derived, not assumed.\n\nTests: hostile-string regressions and mutation-sensitive assertions. I will break the escaping deliberately and confirm the new tests fail, because a green suite proves nothing about coverage.\n\nGates: focused and full Go tests with -race, vet, gofmt, git diff --check. docs/reference/architecture.md only if the layer contract actually changes. Then an exact-head internal/statusview artifact succeeding my live one at e9ec6070, and an independent review request with Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions.\n\nBranch request/terminal-control-neutralization in its own worktree, as the request records.","body":{"area":"internal/statusview","base":"7e7b8412bcd95e3d3345a481b72febc502513109","branch":"request/terminal-control-neutralization","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:712694680912799ba18621f59791f90d099e4c83"}}